  "graph": {
    "id": "unified-example-dice-stakes",
    "name": "Real dice with frozen stakes",
    "description": "Confirm an actual player roll, freeze authored stakes, draw a uniform d20, calculate the bonus and difficulty comparison, guide native narration and append a roll receipt.\n\nSetup: Create public JSON dice-outcomes as []. The example watches an actual physical bronze-d20 roll stated in the player message, with canonical actor mara. Set authored stakes, bonus and difficulty before Send. It does not randomly choose whether an unattempted action happens. Configure eventExtract plus the Decision helper. The accepted ledger retains the same player-roll identity across retries/swipes; deliberately rerolling requires a new action.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
